### Bookify API — sample requests for the Security Inlays demo.
### Run the app with the `dev` profile active first (it seeds the `librarian` / `password` user) -
### e.g. `-Dspring-boot.run.profiles=dev`. Server then listens on port 8081.

@host = http://localhost:8081

### List all books — public, no auth required
GET {{host}}/api/books

### Add a book without auth — Spring Security rejects this before BookController ever runs
POST {{host}}/api/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Refactoring",
  "isbn": "9780134757599"
}

### Same request as the librarian — satisfies the HTTP-level role check, 201 Created
POST {{host}}/api/books
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Basic librarian password

{
  "name": "Refactoring",
  "isbn": "9780134757599"
}

### Delete a book without auth — blocked before BookService.removeBook() runs
DELETE {{host}}/api/books/a0eebc99-9c0b-4ef8-bb6d-6bb9bd380a15

### Same delete as the librarian — satisfies both the HTTP matcher and BookService's @PreAuthorize
DELETE {{host}}/api/books/a0eebc99-9c0b-4ef8-bb6d-6bb9bd380a15
Authorization: Basic librarian password

### Who's currently active? Requires LIBRARIAN — 401 without auth
GET {{host}}/api/members/active

### Same request as the librarian — 200
GET {{host}}/api/members/active
Authorization: Basic librarian password
